1
00:00:00,467 --> 00:00:05,400
Imagine this: you scan a QR code at a shop,
enter one hundred rupees, and type your PIN.

2
00:00:09,967 --> 00:00:12,833
Within seconds, the money reaches the
shopkeeper's bank account.

3
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:20,100
But how do your phone, the payment app, NPCI and two
different banks talk to each other so fast?

4
00:00:22,333 --> 00:00:23,867
How does money move this quickly?

5
00:00:24,833 --> 00:00:28,133
Today, let's understand the technology behind
UPI, step by step.

6
00:00:30,733 --> 00:00:32,600
First, what exactly is UPI?

7
00:00:33,367 --> 00:00:35,900
UPI stands for Unified Payments Interface.

8
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:40,067
It was developed by the National Payments
Corporation of India, or NPCI.

9
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:47,167
UPI is an instant digital payment system that connects different
banks and payment apps through one common network.

10
00:00:52,833 --> 00:00:58,300
Earlier, to send money, you needed the account
number, IFSC code and other bank details.

11
00:01:00,167 --> 00:01:02,333
UPI made this whole process much easier.

12
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:06,800
Now you can pay with a mobile number, a QR
code or a UPI ID.

13
00:01:07,100 --> 00:01:12,400
With a normal UPI payment from your bank account, your
money doesn't need to sit inside the app.

14
00:01:14,567 --> 00:01:18,900
The app simply works as an interface between
your bank account and the UPI network.

15
00:01:20,333 --> 00:01:24,567
To understand a UPI transaction, let's first
look at the key components behind it.

16
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:31,000
First, your smartphone and payment app, where
the transaction starts.

17
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:36,200
Second, the Payment Service Provider, or PSP.

18
00:01:37,767 --> 00:01:40,900
It plays an important role in communicating
with the UPI network.

19
00:01:43,533 --> 00:01:45,933
Third, your bank, called the remitter bank.

20
00:01:46,667 --> 00:01:50,467
Fourth, the receiver's bank, called the
beneficiary bank.

21
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:56,100
And in the middle, NPCI's UPI switch handles
routing and coordination.

22
00:01:59,467 --> 00:02:01,967
All these systems exchange electronic
messages.

23
00:02:03,433 --> 00:02:10,900
So your phone shows just one payment button, but many
financial and technical systems work together behind it.

24
00:02:13,933 --> 00:02:18,900
When you scan a shop's UPI QR code, your payment app
reads the payment information inside it.

25
00:02:20,900 --> 00:02:25,533
This includes the shopkeeper's UPI ID, and
other details depending on the QR type.

26
00:02:27,300 --> 00:02:32,667
Some QR codes already include the amount,
while others ask you to enter it yourself.

27
00:02:33,633 --> 00:02:36,133
Think of a UPI ID as a digital payment
address.

28
00:02:37,567 --> 00:02:42,967
Just as an email address delivers a message to the right
person, a UPI ID routes a payment to the right receiver.

29
00:02:45,967 --> 00:02:51,567
The network resolves this address, so the
payment reaches the correct bank account.

30
00:02:52,433 --> 00:02:57,900
Always check the receiver's name before paying, because money
sent to the wrong person isn't always easy to get back.

31
00:03:01,067 --> 00:03:03,467
Now you enter the amount and type your UPI
PIN.

32
00:03:04,833 --> 00:03:07,067
Your PIN is what authorizes the payment.

33
00:03:07,667 --> 00:03:10,967
It helps your bank confirm that the
transaction is happening with your permission.

34
00:03:14,233 --> 00:03:17,333
As soon as you enter the PIN, the request is
processed securely.

35
00:03:18,700 --> 00:03:22,267
Encryption and secure authentication protect
sensitive information.

36
00:03:24,267 --> 00:03:29,367
Your PIN should never be visible on screen,
and a normal UPI app can't read or store it.

37
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:33,700
Your bank verifies this authentication.

38
00:03:35,367 --> 00:03:40,333
If the PIN is wrong, balance is low, or a security
check fails, the payment can be declined.

39
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:46,033
So your PIN isn't just a password. It's a key
part of transaction authorization.

40
00:03:49,467 --> 00:03:51,300
Now, the most interesting part.

41
00:03:51,533 --> 00:03:53,600
What actually happens behind the scenes?

42
00:03:54,967 --> 00:04:01,033
Say your account has five thousand rupees, and you want to send
one hundred rupees to an account in another bank.

43
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:06,867
First, your payment app starts a payment
request with the required details.

44
00:04:08,200 --> 00:04:11,267
This request goes through the PSP and the UPI
network.

45
00:04:11,867 --> 00:04:17,067
NPCI's UPI switch routes this information, so the
right banks and participants can communicate.

46
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:20,900
Now your bank verifies the transaction.

47
00:04:21,267 --> 00:04:27,133
Authentication, available balance, transaction
limits and security checks are all processed.

48
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:30,900
If every check passes, one hundred rupees is
debited from your account.

49
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:37,467
Then a credit instruction goes through UPI to
the receiver's bank.

50
00:04:38,967 --> 00:04:41,967
The receiver's bank credits one hundred rupees
to their account.

51
00:04:43,933 --> 00:04:47,033
The payment status then travels back through
the network to your app.

52
00:04:48,667 --> 00:04:53,767
As soon as a successful response arrives, your
phone shows Payment Successful.

53
00:04:54,233 --> 00:05:01,400
So behind that simple loading animation, many secure messages,
bank systems and real-time database updates are at work.

54
00:05:05,267 --> 00:05:07,200
So why do we need NPCI?

55
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:10,067
India has many banks and payment apps.

56
00:05:10,500 --> 00:05:14,600
If every app needed its own link to every
bank, things would get very complex.

57
00:05:16,333 --> 00:05:21,100
UPI's common network makes interoperability
possible between banks and payment providers.

58
00:05:22,700 --> 00:05:27,300
NPCI's UPI switch routes transaction messages and
coordinates communication between everyone.

59
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:35,533
Think of it as a smart network junction, sending
each payment message to the right place.

60
00:05:37,267 --> 00:05:41,333
That's why you can send money from one UPI app
to someone using a different UPI app.

61
00:05:42,900 --> 00:05:45,200
You don't need the same bank or the same
payment app.

62
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:50,067
Now the big question: how does this finish in
a few seconds?

63
00:05:51,667 --> 00:05:54,233
The answer: automated payment infrastructure.

64
00:05:54,433 --> 00:06:00,000
When you make a UPI payment, no bank employee
sits and approves each transaction manually.

65
00:06:01,433 --> 00:06:06,167
Connected servers and banking systems process
requests automatically, using set rules.

66
00:06:07,867 --> 00:06:11,233
Secure digital messages move through the
network very fast.

67
00:06:11,467 --> 00:06:18,400
Banking systems verify authentication and balance, and for a
successful transaction, account records are updated.

68
00:06:21,133 --> 00:06:25,533
Electronic communication, automated processing
and standard payment protocols make this fast.

69
00:06:27,933 --> 00:06:31,333
But not every UPI payment will succeed in
exactly two seconds.

70
00:06:32,267 --> 00:06:38,000
Internet connection, server load, bank availability and other
technical conditions can change the processing time.

71
00:06:41,867 --> 00:06:43,900
Now here's something very few people know.

72
00:06:46,267 --> 00:06:52,567
When you pay a customer of another bank, the
receiver can get the credit within seconds.

73
00:06:52,600 --> 00:06:57,633
But crediting a customer's account and settling
between two banks are two separate processes.

74
00:06:59,700 --> 00:07:04,033
Suppose, all day, customers of Bank A make
many payments to customers of Bank B.

75
00:07:06,500 --> 00:07:09,933
And at the same time, Bank B's customers also
pay Bank A's customers.

76
00:07:11,433 --> 00:07:14,133
This creates financial obligations between the
banks.

77
00:07:16,433 --> 00:07:21,967
UPI's settlement system calculates these obligations, and
then the balance is settled between banks.

78
00:07:23,400 --> 00:07:26,533
You can see this with a simple example of net
settlement.

79
00:07:28,167 --> 00:07:32,933
So your payment can complete instantly, while the final
settlement between banks happens separately.

80
00:07:35,667 --> 00:07:39,567
If UPI is so advanced, why do payments
sometimes fail or stay pending?

81
00:07:40,700 --> 00:07:42,100
There can be many reasons.

82
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:51,700
A bank server being temporarily down, a weak internet connection, a wrong
PIN, low balance, a transaction limit, or a technical timeout.

83
00:07:52,900 --> 00:07:57,333
Sometimes money is debited from your account, but the app
doesn't get the final confirmation right away.

84
00:08:00,533 --> 00:08:02,467
Then the transaction may stay pending.

85
00:08:03,233 --> 00:08:05,200
That doesn't mean the money is lost forever.

86
00:08:06,100 --> 00:08:09,533
The network and banks verify the records and
decide the final status.

87
00:08:11,133 --> 00:08:15,700
If the payment really failed and money was debited,
a reversal can happen as per the rules.

88
00:08:18,100 --> 00:08:21,667
So before paying again, check your transaction
history and bank statement.

89
00:08:23,933 --> 00:08:27,500
If needed, contact the official support of
your payment app or bank.

90
00:08:29,267 --> 00:08:33,867
Authentication, protected communication and
bank security checks power UPI security.

91
00:08:35,500 --> 00:08:38,967
But any digital payment system is safest when
the user stays alert too.

92
00:08:40,533 --> 00:08:45,700
First, never share your PIN, OTP or bank
password with anyone.

93
00:08:45,733 --> 00:08:50,100
In a normal UPI transfer, you don't need a PIN
to receive money.

94
00:08:51,800 --> 00:08:58,233
If someone asks you to scan a QR code and enter your PIN for a
refund, cashback or reward, verify everything first.

95
00:09:00,100 --> 00:09:02,100
Don't trust a payment screenshot alone.

96
00:09:03,700 --> 00:09:06,067
Check the real status in your bank account or
app.

97
00:09:07,367 --> 00:09:10,133
Before paying, verify the receiver's name and
amount.

98
00:09:10,933 --> 00:09:15,133
Technology makes payments easy, but staying
alert is just as important for security.

99
00:09:17,533 --> 00:09:23,300
So the next time you scan a QR code at a shop, you'll know how much
advanced infrastructure works behind your phone screen.

100
00:09:26,500 --> 00:09:32,900
One small payment button starts secure communication between
your app, the PSP, the NPCI network and the banks.

101
00:09:34,700 --> 00:09:41,433
Your bank authenticates the payment, the amount is debited, the receiver's
bank processes the credit, and the status comes back to your phone.

102
00:09:45,300 --> 00:09:51,433
Through all these coordinated processes, UPI
makes digital payments fast and convenient.

103
00:09:53,300 --> 00:09:59,433
That's why, from small shops to online
shopping, UPI is now part of our daily life.

104
00:10:00,133 --> 00:10:04,500
A payment that starts with a simple QR code is
the story of a huge financial network.

105
00:10:06,167 --> 00:10:12,267
If you enjoy understanding the systems behind technology, like this
video, and subscribe for more technology documentaries.

106
00:10:15,300 --> 00:10:17,333
See you in the next video. Thank you!
